IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Superannuation (Distribution of Surplus) Act 1974 (Cth). Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00074.txt. Seat: the contributor or
-- pensioner.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Fund member` HAS
    -- s 3(1) "eligible contributor"
    `obliged to contribute before 1 July 1972`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contributor on 11 April 1974`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `became a pensioner on`                             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `died while a contributor on`                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `left a widow or eligible children`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `deferred benefits applicable by 30 June 1972`      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(2)
    `deferred benefits not yet payable on 30 June 1972` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(1) "eligible pensioner": a pension (not non-contributory) payable or
    -- suspended at some time between 1 July 1962 and 30 June 1972
    `a contributory pension in the relevant period`     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6(2)
    `died before payment`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `widow alive at payment`                            IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Who is paid` IS ONE OF
    `the member`
    `the widow`
    `whoever the Board determines`
    `no one: not eligible`

§ `Rules`

`the relevant period starts` MEANS Date 1 7 1962
`the relevant period ends` MEANS Date 30 6 1972
`assent` MEANS Date 11 4 1974

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the window` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT LEAST `the relevant period starts` AND d LESS THAN `assent`

-- s 3(1) "eligible contributor".
@ref s 3(1)
GIVEN f IS A `Fund member`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible contributor` f IF
        f's `obliged to contribute before 1 July 1972`
    AND NOT (f's `deferred benefits applicable by 30 June 1972`)
    AND (    f's `a contributor on 11 April 1974`
         OR  `within the window` (f's `became a pensioner on`)
         OR (`within the window` (f's `died while a contributor on`) AND f's `left a widow or eligible children`))

-- s 3(1)-(2) "eligible pensioner".
@ref s 3(1)-(2)
GIVEN f IS A `Fund member`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible pensioner` f IF
        f's `a contributory pension in the relevant period`
    OR  f's `deferred benefits not yet payable on 30 June 1972`

-- s 6: payment to the member; if dead before payment, to the widow if alive,
-- otherwise as the Board determines.
@ref ss 3, 6
@export default Am I entitled to a share of the 1972 surplus of the Superannuation Fund under the Superannuation (Distribution of Surplus) Act 1974 (Cth), and who is paid? An eligible contributor or eligible pensioner (s 3) is entitled to the share the Treasurer allocates (s 5); it is paid to them, or, if they died before payment, to their widow if alive, otherwise to whoever the Board determines (s 6). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Fund member`  @desc The member's contribution and pension history, and any death before payment
GIVETH A `Who is paid`
`who is paid the share of` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an eligible contributor` f OR `an eligible pensioner` f) THEN `no one: not eligible`
        IF NOT (f's `died before payment`)                                 THEN `the member`
        IF f's `widow alive at payment`                                    THEN `the widow`
        OTHERWISE                                                               `whoever the Board determines`
